desc:
Ten big brave army men toting carbines;
One shot himself and then there were nine.
Nine big brave army men awaiting fate;
Eight big brave army men under fiery Heaven;
The fire blinded one and then there were seven.
Seven big brave army men afeared of the phoenix;
One got burned and then there were six.
Six big brave army men trying to survive;
Rads sickened one and then there were five.
Five big brave army men contemplating war;
Four big brave army men bunking in a tree;
One had a fall and then there were three.
Three big brave army men fighting over stew;
One shot another and then there were two.
Two big brave army men starving in the sun;
One hanged himself and then there was one.
One big brave army man left all alone;
He sighed and cried, but followed the road...
